# L §3.3 (round 6): factor "otherwise needs to u (§7.3), LOAD-TO where load can't show the power is an integer": over
# a month, t is 1/12, 1/3 or 1 by r's period, which load doesn't see (r is an input), so the power t·n isn't shown to
# be an integer, though n is an int: refused at load.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input r: rate
input n12: int
def f: num = factor(r, n12, month, effective) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  r = 12 %/year
  n12 = 12

ask b: f law 2026-06-30
=== expect
refused: LOAD-TO ...
